invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: message_mod_prime returns without wiping r3, which holds R^3
  modulo the prime: a public number modulo a prime, which with that
  number gives the prime. Inside a signature a later call's frame is
  written over that one, so bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test calls the reduction
  on its own (test/rsa_sign_equiv_pieces.c), copies the stack below it
  and finds two words of the value there.

--- old
    ct_wipe(high, sizeof high);
    ct_wipe(r3, sizeof r3);
--- new
    ct_wipe(high, sizeof high);
